faq:
  - q: "How often should my books be updated?"
    a: "Most small businesses do well with monthly bookkeeping. If you have fewer transactions, quarterly can work. We'll recommend a schedule that fits your business."
  - q: "What payroll tax filings do New York employers have?"
    a: "Most employers file federal Form 941 every quarter and Form 940 once a year, New York State Form NYS-45 every quarter, and W-2s for employees at year end. Payroll taxes also have to be deposited on a regular schedule. We keep track of all of it."
  - q: "Do I need bookkeeping if I'm a sole proprietor?"
    a: "It helps. Keeping business and personal spending separate and recording it through the year makes your Schedule C accurate and supports every deduction you claim."
